id: pm-kmnvug
title: Surface replication gate activates unrelated sets through shared required members
description: "Changing a shared documentation or test member activates every replication set that requires it, even when none of that set's explicit trigger files changed. This forces unrelated source churn and defeats the distinction between triggers and required changed members."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-08T16:08:23.450Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-08T16:50:20.983Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-08T16:50:09.771Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-08T16:50:09.771Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 2
acceptance_criteria: Only declared trigger files activate a replication set;Once activated every required changed member is still enforced;Regression test proves shared non-trigger members do not activate unrelated sets
parent: pm-doxj
resolution: fixed
expected_result: "Only explicitly declared trigger files activate a replication set; after activation, every required member remains mandatory and shared non-trigger files cannot activate unrelated sets."
actual_result: "The surface-replication gate now activates a contract set only through explicit trigger files; once active it still enforces every required member, preventing unrelated shared members from creating false activation failures."
